%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a0711db1b03ce448c93419c25aa574d8, type: 3}
  m_Name: Cassette AI
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogLines:
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: "If you\u2019re listening to this... then it has already happened.
      The world we knew is gone. I\u2019m recording this because there\u2019s no
      time left\u2014and because someone needs to know what we did."
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6d6f6ad9704c040bc96b93c3271cb8fb, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: For years, global leaders abandoned every climate agreement. In the
      race for power and growth, the planet was stripped of its last resources. The
      air turned toxic. Breathing became a privilege.
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6696d5bd6870e4ebaaf7bcf4464446db, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: We needed a radical solution. That solution was the Resonance Project.
      I helped design it. We believed we could save the world by using resonance
      waves to push contaminants away from populated areas. And for a while... it
      worked. The data was perfect. The air felt cleaner. We truly believed we had
      succeeded.
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 59af27709813c4451a02311fc732ee66, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: "But we failed to predict the consequences. Resonance didn\u2019t
      destroy the pollution; it concentrated it\u2014in places we never expected,
      at levels no classical simulation could describe. Unknown physical phenomena:
      non-linear resonance, phase collapse, matter entanglement... it turned contamination
      into something alive."
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2e2e4eb2978f04dfcb5ed720defe3438, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: The creatures didn't come from the outside. We created them.
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8253e4fe5d48b49fdb67c7f91eb8469e, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: My name is Kael. I am the chief engineer of The Factory, the core
      of the Resonance Project. When I realized what was happening, I tried to stop
      it. I brought models, data, projections. They silenced me. Too much politics.
      Too many interests.
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7dbb446c6561348bcad3a365b8fbd223, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: "That\u2019s why I\u2019m using a cassette. Every digital channel
      was monitored. This... they can\u2019t erase."
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 971c833e0c5eb47a39901efe4dfa7666, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: "Listen carefully: These creatures go for light. It destabilizes
      their structure and drives them into a frenzy. In darkness, they are blind
      and less aggressive, but they can still hear us. They don\u2019t perceive the
      world the way we do. What they hear and see is different."
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b5c37af9982f6470697d42413aa78826, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: "I don\u2019t have time to explain everything, but there is a solution.
      I called it The Zero Note. It\u2019s not a single frequency; it\u2019s a superposition.
      A cancellation. I\u2019ve hidden the clues inside my research, in systems they
      didn't isolate. You\u2019ll have to find them."
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3babb3e5ab7ef469c99cf16051412971, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: "If it\u2019s you listening, Noah... you\u2019re the most brilliant
      engineer I\u2019ve ever known. Recalibrate the Towers. Find the Zero Note."
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 65f971f53a5c14a0cb3ad5ce5966f9a3, type: 3}
  - speakerName: Kael
    dialogText: I have to go now. Good luck.
    audioClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 72de9943c7dd94bceb06c5785d768cae, type: 3}
